The bug causing failures in [`winzipBackSlashWorkaround`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/compress_13_group_a_blind/src/test/java/org/apache/commons/compress/archivers/zip/ZipArchiveInputStreamTest.java#L35) and [`testWinzipBackSlashWorkaround`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/compress_13_group_a_blind/src/test/java/org/apache/commons/compress/archivers/zip/ZipFileTest.java#L145) has been identified and fixed.

### Root Cause
Zip archives created on Windows/FAT file systems (e.g. by WinZip) can contain file names that use backslashes (`\`) instead of forward slashes (`/`) as directory separators. When reading such entries, [`ZipArchiveEntry.setName(String)`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/compress_13_group_a_blind/src/main/java/org/apache/commons/compress/archivers/zip/ZipArchiveEntry.java#L511) stored the path with backslashes verbatim instead of normalizing them to forward slashes.

### Fix
Updated [`ZipArchiveEntry.setName(String)`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/compress_13_group_a_blind/src/main/java/org/apache/commons/compress/archivers/zip/ZipArchiveEntry.java#L511) to normalize backslashes to forward slashes when the platform is `PLATFORM_FAT` and no forward slashes are present in the entry name:

```java
    protected void setName(String name) {
        if (name != null && getPlatform() == PLATFORM_FAT
            && name.indexOf("/") == -1) {
            name = name.replace('\\', '/');
        }
        this.name = name;
    }
```

